                        "entry_id": "cc864fda-6e62-3424-bad3-c2786f863cab",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of derivatives of barbituric acid that act as depressants of the central nervous system and are used as sedatives or hypnotics."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c3fd57c1-6e08-4cb4-8efc-cc6193587d46",
                                "sense_id": "735525ad-4e64-36d7-834f-429dd8fb6689",
                                "text": "Following the “Summer of Love” in 1967, amphetamines and barbiturates began to replace psychedelics as the dominant drugs used in the Haight-Ashbury district of San Francisco, and increasing numbers of individuals were treated at the Haight-Ashbury Free Medical Clinic for complications following barbiturate use."
                            }
                        ]
